    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/964263?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral researcher in learning, control, and games",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoctoral researcher in learning, control, and games Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoctoral researcher in learning, control, and games KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Job description We are looking for a highly motivated postdoctoral researcher with a strong interest in intelligent systems in which artificial intelligence, human decision-making, or both interact with dynamical environments. The successful candidate is expected to have a solid background in one or more of the following areas: applied mathematics, systems and control, game theory, machine learning, optimization, and decision-making. The project seeks to develop mathematical foundations and computational methods for the analysis, learning, and coordination of complex closed-loop systems involving three tightly coupled components: a dynamical environment, algorithmic decision makers, and strategic or adaptive agents. In such systems, decisions influence not only the physical environment but also the behavior of other participants and the data subsequently available for learning. These feedback effects create fundamental challenges for stability, identifiability, performance, and robustness that cannot be addressed by treating learning, control, and strategic interaction separately. The research will investigate how these coupled systems can be modeled, analyzed, and designed to achieve reliable system-level outcomes. The broader objective is to use insights from closed-loop decision-making to design intelligent systems that are more efficient, sustainable, resilient, and reliable. The selected candidates will also be enrolled in the Wallenberg AI, Autonomous Systems, and Software Program ( WASP ), thereby gaining privileged access to its extensive resources. The WASP is Sweden’s largest individual research program ever, a major national initiative for strategically motivated basic research, education, and faculty recruitment. The program addresses research on artificial intelligence and autonomous systems acting in collaboration with humans, adapting to their environment through sensors, information, and knowledge, and forming intelligent systems-of-systems. The vision of WASP is excellent research and competence in artificial intelligence, autonomous systems, and software for the benefit of the Swedish industry. The workplace The Department of Mathematics ( https://www.kth.se/math ) has vibrant research environment, featuring world-class groups in applied, computational, and pure mathematics, as well as mathematical statistics. The research group excels in optimization and mathematical systems theory, with particular emphasis on network and nonlinear control and games, numerical analysis, optimization with particular emphasis on large-scale nonlinear programming and a range of applications. With a strong tradition of collaboration, the group works closely with startups, industry leaders, and academic institutions across Sweden and Europe, driving innovation and impactful research. Notable industrial projects span robotics, radiation therapy, cell biology, and supply chain optimization. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. A strong foundation in mathematical tools relevant to the project. A demonstrated record of exceptional research achievements and publications in high-impact venues. Advanced analytical skills, with a proven ability to work independently and collaboratively within interdisciplinary teams. Outstanding communication skills, both written and verbal, to effectively disseminate research findings and collaborate with team members. Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Expertise in one or more of the specific research areas relevant to the position. Teaching and mentoring abilities. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. A complete application packet includes the following items: CV including research areas and a publication list. Cover letter (1 page max). A statement of current research and future research plans (2 page max except for references). Copy of diplomas and grades from all your previous university studies. (Translations into English or Swedish if the original ones are not in any of these languages.) The contact information of at least 3 professional references, including their email addresses, phone numbers, and affiliations. The references may be contacted during the evaluation process. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2916 Published 02.Sep.2026 Last application date 16.Oct.2026 Contact Silun Zhang silunz@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/969641?l=en": {
      "title": "Research Engineer in Soft and Wearable Robotics",
      "description": "KTH | Research Engineer in Soft and Wearable Robotics kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Research Engineer in Soft and Wearable Robotics KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Job description The Robot Design Lab at the Mechatronics Division at KTH is searching for a research engineer in the field of robot design and mechatronics with focus on soft and wearable robotics. The position is part of the ongoing flagship REMA project, Redefining Mobility for Aging Adults, which aims to develop new exoskeleton technologies for aging adults through the integration of soft robotics, sensing, actuation, adaptive control, and user-centered design. The research engineer will contribute to the design, development, integration, and experimental evaluation of soft exoskeletons and their mechatronic systems. The work will span the development of soft robotic structures, sensing and actuation systems, mechanical and electromechanical integration, control, and the realization of functional robotic prototypes. The work will include iterative development, assembly, verification, and validation through simulation and experimental testing. The research engineer will also participate in the planning and execution of experiments, analysis of results, student supervision, and dissemination of the research through scientific publications in relevant international conferences and journals. Qualifications Requirements MSc degree in robotics, mechatronics, electrical engineering, mechanical engineering or equivalent. Experience in mechanical design and CAD software, such as SolidWorks, Autodesk Inventor, Autodesk Fusion 360, Solid Edge, or equivalent, Experience in additive manufacturing (3D printing), prototyping, and assembly of robotic or mechatronic systems·. Good programming skills in MATLAB and/or Python. Experience in the integration and control of electrical motors and actuators in robotic or mechatronic systems. Experience in experimental testing, verification, and validation of robotic or mechatronic prototypes. Relevant scientific publications in international conferences and/or journals. Good ability to communicate in English both verbally and in writing, as it is required in the daily work. Solid academic record and well-developed problem-solving skills. Ability to work both independently and in a group, Preferred qualifications Experience in wearable robotics, exoskeletons, soft robotics, or physical human-robot interaction. Experience in sensors, signal processing, and sensor integration for robotic or mechatronic systems. Experience in automatic control theory and implementation, including motion and/or force control. Experience in actuator and transmission design, including cable-driven or compliant mechanisms. Experience in robot or multibody simulation software, such as Simscape Multibody, Gazebo, Webots, or CoppeliaSim. Knowledge of Finite Element (FE) simulation of mechanical parts and assemblies. Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Cover letter: a brief description (maximum 2 pages) of why you want to conduct research at the Robot Design Lab at KTH Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to one year, with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment As soon as possible or according to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3114 Published 18.Sep.2026 Last application date 17.Oct.2026 Contact Georgios Andrikopoulos geoand@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/963604?l=en": {
      "title": "Doctoral student in Remote Fault Attacks on Cryptographic Algorithms",
      "description": "KTH | Doctoral student in Remote Fault Attacks on Cryptographic Algorithms kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Doctoral student in Remote Fault Attacks on Cryptographic Algorithms KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Electrical Engineering and Computer Science Project description Third-cycle subject: Information and Communication Technology Currently, there are no effective methods for protecting implementations of cryptographic algorithms from fault attacks, where an adversary deliberately injects faults into cryptographic computations to extract sensitive information. This project aims to address this important open problem, with a particular focus on remote attacks. We intend to take into account the impact of fault attacks on cryptographic implementation security from both an offensive perspective (by devising new types of attacks) and a defensive perspective (by designing countermeasures). The overarching challenge is to create defense mechanisms that can withstand fault attacks as the adversary's capabilities grow. By considering mathematical and electrical engineering problems together, the project is expected to create cryptographic implementations in which resistance to fault attacks is incorporated at the design stage rather than addressed later, after a vulnerability is discovered. The successful candidate is expected to investigate the use of advanced machine learning techniques to enhance both the analysis and mitigation of fault attacks. The insights gained will be used to develop new vulnerability assessment methods and design countermeasures against fault attacks, along with supporting tools. The work will be carried out in the Hardware Security group at KTH which currently includes five PhD students. The project is funded by the Swedish Research Council. Supervision: Prof. Elena Dubrova and Prof. Carl-Mikael Zetterling Admission requirements To be admitted to postgraduate education (Chapter 7, 39 § Swedish Higher Education Ordinance), the applicant must have basic eligibility in accordance with either of the following: passed a second cycle degree (for example a master's degree), or completed course requirements of at least 240 higher education credits, of which at least 60 second-cycle higher education credits, or acquired, in some other way within or outside the country, substantially equivalent knowledge The special eligibility requirements include knowledge of cryptographic algorithms, expertise fault and side-channel attacks, experience in embedded systems, as well as practical skills in machine learning including knowledge of essentials tools and platforms such as TensorFlow, etc. In addition to the above, there is also a mandatory requirement for English equivalent to English B/6. Selection In order to succeed as a doctoral student at KTH you need to be goal oriented and persevering in your work. During the selection process, candidates will be assessed upon their ability to: independently pursue his or her work collaborate with others, have a professional approach, analyze and work with complex issues and communicate research results effectively in writing and through presentations Applicants who have completed a course in hardware security as part of their academic curriculum will be given a priority. Applicants whose bachelor/master thesis work was performed in the area of hardware security will be given a priority. Applicants with published papers in high-ranked hardware security journals, conferences, or workshops will be given a priority. After the qualification requirements, great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Target degree: Doctoral degree Information regarding admission and employment Only those admitted to postgraduate education may be employed as a doctoral student. The total length of employment may not be longer than what corresponds to full-time doctoral education in four years' time. An employed doctoral student can, to a limited extent (maximum 20%), perform certain tasks within their role, e.g. training and administration. A new position as a doctoral student is for a maximum of one year, and then the employment may be renewed for a maximum of two years at a time. As a doctoral student, you are entitled to a workplace with many employee benefits and monthly salary according to KTH’s Doctoral student salary agreement . Read more about Doctoral studies (PhD) | KTH | Sweden . Union representatives Contact information for union representatives. Doctoral Student’s network (Students’ union on KTH Royal Institute of Technology) Contact information for PhD chapter . To apply for the position Apply for the position and admission through KTH's recruitment system. It is the applicant’s responsibility to ensure that the application is complete in accordance with the instructions in the advertisement. Applications must include the following elements: Copies of diplomas and grades from previous university studies and certificates of fulfilled language requirements (see above) . Translations into English or Swedish if the original document is not issued in one of these languages.Copies of originals must be certified . CV including your relevant professional experience and knowledge. Application letter with a brief description of why you want to pursue research studies, about what your academic interests are and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. (Maximum 2 pages long) Representative publications or technical reports. For longer documents, please provide a summary (abstract) and a web link to the full text. Applications must be received at the last closing date at midnight, CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary according to KTH's doctoral student salary agreement Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2888 Published 03.Sep.2026 Last application date 17.Oct.2026 Contact Elena Dubrova dubrova@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
