    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/983033?l=en": {
      "title": "Researcher in data driven health, with specialisation in knowledge graphs",
      "description": "KTH | Researcher in data driven health, with specialisation in knowledge graphs Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Researcher in data driven health, with specialisation in knowledge graphs School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health at KTH Job description Within the department, we run a large number of research projects in close collaboration with societal stakeholders, with the aim of creating value from health data at the societal, individual, and health care levels. Data harmonization, the use of knowledge graphs, visualization, and participatory methods are key competencies for developing meaningful projects. The department has many students, and we are seeking a researcher who can build successful initiatives that connect societal stakeholders’ expectations with the collective expertise of our students. We see integrating education with research as an important way to create impact. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree You have demonstrated research expertise in computer science in the health domain or a related field. You have experience leading research projects in collaboration with societal stakeholders, particularly in the public sector on health-related issues. You can lead and develop projects involving health data, and have extensive experience working with knowledge graphs, cloud services, and Kubernetes environments. You take a pedagogical approach and have the skills needed to include master’s students in your projects. You work independently and can collaborate with a wide range of professionals to achieve impact through your research. Preferred qualifications Familiarity with Swedish open data sources in the public sector, particularly those related to health and social care, is an advantage. Knowledge of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH . Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max two pages long. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 12 months, with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3655 Published 24.Oct.2026 Last application date 02.Nov.2026 Contact Sebastiaan Meijer smeijer@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/982979?l=en": {
      "title": ": Researcher in computational magnetism and spintronics",
      "description": "KTH | : Researcher in computational magnetism and spintronics Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies : Researcher in computational magnetism and spintronics School of Engineering Sciences at KTH Job description The Department of Applied Physics is seeking a researcher in theoretical and computational magnetism and spintronics. The position is placed in an internationally prominent research group at the AlbaNova University Center, studying magnetic materials and spin phenomena using advanced computational methods. You will conduct research on magnetic and spintronic phenomena in quantum materials and low-dimensional systems, for example spin and magnon transport, fundamental magnetic interactions, and topological spin textures in two-dimensional magnets, antiferromagnets and altermagnets. The work includes the development and application of first-principles calculations, atomistic spin dynamics and micromagnetic simulations, as well as the development of automated and AI-assisted computational workflows for large-scale materials studies. The duties also include supervising doctoral students and postdocs, collaborating with experimental and theoretical research groups in Sweden and internationally, actively seeking external research funding, and contributing to the scientific environment of the group and the department. Some teaching and pedagogical qualification may be included in the duties. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree Documented research expertise in theoretical or computational condensed matter physics with a focus on magnetism and spintronics, demonstrated through publications in leading international scientific journals. Extensive experience of electronic structure calculations (first principles/DFT) and of simulating magnetic materials and their properties. Excellent command of English, spoken and written, as the work is carried out in an international research environment. As a person, you are independent and driven, and you have excellent collaborative abilities. Preferred qualifications Documented experience of research on fundamental magnetic interactions, for example the Dzyaloshinskii–Moriya interaction, magnetic anisotropy and exchange interactions, and their role in topological magnetism. Experience of studies of spin and magnon transport in two-dimensional magnets, van der Waals materials, antiferromagnets or altermagnets. Experience of atomistic spin dynamics and micromagnetic simulations. Experience of machine learning/AI and of developing automated workflows for large-scale calculations on high-performance computing resources. A documented ability to attract external research funding in competition, as well as scientific prizes and awards. Teaching ability and experience of supervising doctoral students or postdocs. The ability to work towards research results being utilised in practice and to inform about research and development work. Experience of developing and leading activities and staff. Knowledge of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with a specific focus on gender equality. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH . Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max two pages long. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid until further notice (permanent post) according to agreement. The employment begins with a six-month probationary period. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3652 Published 27.Oct.2026 Last application date 05.Nov.2026 Contact Anna Delin annadel@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/981265?l=en": {
      "title": "Research engineer in experimental aerodynamics for turbomachinery",
      "description": "KTH | Research engineer in experimental aerodynamics for turbomachinery kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Research engineer in experimental aerodynamics for turbomachinery KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Job description Division of Heat and Power Technology at the Department of Energy Technology is seeking a Research Engineer to conduct research within the Vinnova-funded projects “Impact of INlet DIstortion on the AEROdynamic and AEROelastic characteristics of an axial compressor stage (INDIAERO)” and “AI Supported Adaptive Manufacturing (AISAM)”. The projects address two important aspects affecting the aerodynamic and aeromechanical performance of fan and compressor blades in aero-engines: blade erosion and inlet flow distortion. Leading-edge erosion can increase aerodynamic losses and consequently fuel consumption. At the same time, aero-engines are frequently exposed to non-uniform inlet flow conditions due to intake geometry and varying flight conditions. These distortions can affect both aerodynamic performance and aeroelastic stability, potentially leading to phenomena such as flutter and high-cycle fatigue. Reliable methods for assessing these effects are still under development and constitute an active area of international research. High-quality experimental data are essential for the development and validation of such methods. The work will include the development and design of experimental test setups, detailed aerodynamic measurements, and the analysis and comparison of experimental and numerical results. The position involves close collaboration with the industrial partners participating in the projects. In addition to research activities, the position may include teaching and other education-related activities corresponding to up to 10% of the working time.. Qualifications Requirements To qualify for the position, you must hold a Master of Science degree in Energy Technology, Aerospace Engineering, Mechanical Engineering, Fluid Mechanics, or an equivalent field. You must have a good knowledge of turbomachinery aerodynamics, demonstrated through relevant academic programmes/courses and/or professional experience. Research expertise Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Collaborative abilities Independence Preferred qualifications Experience in experimental testing and design of aerodynamic experiments is considered particularly meritorious. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max one page long. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 12 months, with access according to agreement. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Special fixed-term employment Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment November 1, 2026 or according to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3613 Published 21.Oct.2026 Last application date 06.Nov.2026 Contact Nenad Glodic nenad.glodic@energy.kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/978110?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoctor in purification of graphite for lithium-ion batteries",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoctor in purification of graphite for lithium-ion batteries kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoctor in purification of graphite for lithium-ion batteries KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health Job description At the department of chemical engineering, research is conducted with the common objective to develop sustainable processes. We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher to work in a project focusing on purification of natural graphite for use in batteries. The work is part of a collaboration project with the objective to develop both thermal and chemical processes for this purpose. At KTH the work is focused on developing sustainable chemical processes. The work includes design and experimental studies of simple model systems as well as applied studies in collaboration with the other project partners. The applicant should have extensive experience in laboratory work and is expected to be able to work both independently and in collaboration with colleagues at KTH and other organizations. The project is led by RISE and is a collaboration between RISE, KTH and Uppsala University, funded by the Swedish Energy Agency. This is a full-time position for two years. The start date is open for discussion. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree in chemistry, chemical engineering, material science. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline We are looking for motivated individuals who can contribute with their own ideas and who can work both independently and as part of a group. Great emphasis will be placed on personal competency. Expertise in chemical engineering and/or hydrometallurgy. Strong academic credentials and scientific proficiency documented in publications. Curiosity, drive and ability to maintain a well-organized work environment. Strong laboratory/instrumental skills An analytical approach Excellent written and oral communication skills in English Teaching abilities Teamwork Independence Awareness of diversity and equal treatment issues with a particular focus on gender equality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3468 Published 19.Oct.2026 Last application date 09.Nov.2026 Contact Kerstin Forsberg kerstino@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/982960?l=en": {
      "title": "Research Engineer in experimental physics.",
      "description": "KTH | Research Engineer in experimental physics. kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Research Engineer in experimental physics. KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Job description You will work as a research engineer within the Quantum Materials group and assist the members of the group in developing the experimental setups that the group runs. Specifically, you will work with the design and development of mechanical components for the various experiments as well as maintenance and fault rectification. Qualifications Requirements A graduate degree or an advanced level (higher education) in a relevant subject or equivalent competence. Documented experience in mechanical design and experience with CAD. Substantial experience of practical technical work As a person, you are service-oriented and find it easy to collaborate. You are at the same time self-motivated and goal-oriented with the ability to drive projects all the way to implementation. You have a broad interest in technology and a willingness to learn new subjects and techniques. Preferred qualifications We would like you to have experience of working with precision mechanics and workshop work such as the use of lathes, milling machines, NC machines, etc. We would also like you to have experience in one or several of the topics optics and optical design, high-power lasers, vacuum technology and cryotechnology. It is also a merit if you have experience of working with software control of hardware as well as working in multicultural environments and awareness of diversity and equal treatment issues with a particular focus on gender equality. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Three examples of parts or mechanical systems designed with CAD. Brief account of your motivations for applying, expectations and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid until further notice (permanent post) according to agreement. The employment begins with a six-month probationary period . Other information Striving towards gender equality, diversity and equal conditions is both a question of quality for KTH and a given part of our values. For information about the processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment Enligt överenskommelse Salary Månadslön Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3647 Published 23.Oct.2026 Last application date 13.Nov.2026 Contact Oscar Tjernberg oscar@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/977770?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in multi-omics machine learning and computational cancer biology",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in multi-omics machine learning and computational cancer biology Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in multi-omics machine learning and computational cancer biology KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health Job Description The lab is part of the SciLifeLab and Wallenberg National Program for Data-Driven Life Science (DDLS) and is based at SciLifeLab Stockholm and KTH. We develop and apply computational approaches for cancer precision medicine , with a particular focus on understanding the molecular mechanisms underlying cancer aggressiveness, metastasis and treatment resistance. The research combines cancer biology, multi-omics and computational methods, with a strong track record of interdisciplinary research and publications in leading journals. More information about the lab is available at: A Lundberg Lab. We will integrate multiple data modalities (biological, clinical/pathological data and medical imaging), with an emphasis on developing interpretable and biologically meaningful models . Methods include machine/deep learning, image analysis, computational pathology, multi-omics integration and foundation models . The position is suitable for a researcher with a strong computational background and demonstrated expertise in machine learning, deep learning or related areas , combined with an interest in cancer biology and biomedical applications. The position also includes opportunities to contribute to grant applications, research networks, education and mentorship. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree in computer science, machine learning, computational biology, bioinformatics, or a related field. This eligibility requirement must be fulfilled by the time the appointment decision is made. A strong research profile in machine learning, deep learning, computational biology, or related computational fields, with a demonstrated interest in applying computational methods to cancer or other biomedical research. Programming skills in Python and/or R, and experience developing, implementing, and evaluating computational or machine learning methods. Solid knowledge of statistics, biostatistics, and multivariate data analysis, including appropriate methods for model evaluation and validation. Excellent written and spoken English, as English is used in day-to-day work. Experience in: Working with large-scale, high-dimensional biological or biomedical datasets and integrating heterogeneous data types. One or more of the following areas: multi-omics data analysis and integration, multimodal machine learning, medical imaging, computational pathology, image analysis, biological data integration, or foundation models. Unix/Linux environments and high-performance computing systems. Scientific writing, scientific publications, and/or grant applications. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree obtained within the three years preceding the application deadline. Experience in: Developing interpretable or explainable machine learning models. Applying machine learning to cancer biology, cancer genomics, or precision medicine. Working with large-scale public or clinical datasets and independently developing research projects. Teaching, mentoring, or supervision. Well-developed analytical and problem-solving skills. Ability to work effectively in an interdisciplinary and collaborative research environment. A structured and organized working style. Awareness of diversity and equal opportunities, with a particular focus on gender equality. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief description of why you want to conduct research in A Lundberg lab, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3456 Published 26.Oct.2026 Last application date 15.Nov.2026 Contact Arian Lundberg arianl@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/980986?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in ICME for electron beam powder bed fusion",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in ICME for electron beam powder bed fusion Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in ICME for electron beam powder bed fusion KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Job description At KTH Royal Institute of Technology, XPRES (the Centre of Excellence in Production Research) is a long-term national initiative to strengthen production science. Established in 2010, XPRES brings together KTH, Mälardalen University, RISE, and Swerim in close collaboration with leading industry to advance sustainable, digitalized, and human-centric manufacturing. We now invite outstanding candidates to join this dynamic, multi-partner research environment as postdoctoral researchers. We are looking for a postdoctoral researcher to advance the understanding of process-microstructure-property relationships in metal additive manufacturing, with a focus on electron beam powder bed fusion (PBF-EB). The project investigates how process strategy, geometry and thermal history influence local microstructure and material properties in complex components. Using an Integrated Computational Materials Engineering (ICME) approach, modeling, process data and experimental characterization will be combined to link processing conditions to material behavior and structural integrity. Depending on your background, the work may include materials, process and microstructure modeling, process-data analysis, materials characterization and mechanical testing. The project is based at the Department of Materials Science and Engineering and carried out within XPRES, in close collaboration with researchers in materials science, structural mechanics and production engineering. You will have the opportunity to shape the scientific direction and develop new methods at the interface between these fields. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. Research expertise in materials science, materials engineering, mechanical engineering, manufacturing engineering or another field relevant to the project. Demonstrated research experience in metallic materials and additive manufacturing, rapid solidification, computational materials science, materials modelling or a closely related area. Experience of connecting computational or theoretical approaches with experimental data or materials characterization. Ability to independently formulate and address scientific research questions. Good collaborative abilities and an interest in working across disciplinary boundaries. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline. Experience with Integrated Computational Materials Engineering (ICME), CALPHAD, microstructure modelling, process modelling, or related computational method. Experience with powder bed fusion or other metal additive manufacturing processes. Experience of combining modeling and experiments in materials research. Scientific publications demonstrating a high level of research expertise. Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3575 Published 21.Oct.2026 Last application date 20.Nov.2026 Contact Greta Lindwall gretal@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/966417?l=en": {
      "title": "Associate Prof. in Industrial informatics for production engineering",
      "description": "KTH | Associate Prof. in Industrial informatics for production engineering Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Associate Prof. in Industrial informatics for production engineering KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Subject field Industrial informatics for Production engineering. Subject description Industrial Informatics for Production Engineering is an interdisciplinary field focusing on the development, integration, and use of digital information systems and information flows to support the planning, development, and continuous improvement of industrial production systems and value chains. The field addresses industrial applications where a lifecycle perspective, systems integration, and the role of people within the system are central. Duties The position encompasses research, teaching, and collaboration within the field of Industrial Informatics for Production Engineering. The Associate Professor is expected to develop internationally competitive research and contribute to further developing the field at KTH. This includes initiating and leading research projects, securing external research funding, developing national and international collaborations, supervising doctoral students and postdoctoral researchers, and actively contributing to the research environment at the department and KTH. The interdisciplinary nature of the field entails close collaboration with research groups in production engineering, digitalisation, automation, computer science, and sustainable development, as well as with industry and other societal stakeholders. The position also includes teaching and pedagogical development at undergraduate, graduate, and doctoral levels. Teaching may include the Bachelor of Science in Industrial Engineering, the Master of Science in Mechanical Engineering, and the master's programmes Production Engineering and Management and Sustainable Production Development. Duties include course responsibility, course development, teaching, and supervision of degree projects and doctoral students. The Associate Professor is also expected to contribute to the development of lifelong learning activities and to the integration of current research into education. In addition, the Associate Professor is expected to contribute to the development of digital research and educational environments, laboratories, and demonstration facilities within the field, and to actively collaborate with industry and public-sector organisations to strengthen the relevance and impact of research and education. The Associate Professor is expected to be able to teach in Swedish within three years. Where required, an individual language development plan will be established in connection with the appointment. Eligibility Those eligible to be employed as associate professor are persons who have: have completed a doctorate or possess equivalent scientific expertise or some other professional expertise that is of significance with regard to the subject content of the employment and the duties that are required of the employment, and demonstrated pedagogical expertise. Assessment criteria The assessment criteria for appointment as an associate professor at KTH shall be the degree of expertise required as a qualification for employment. In addition, the assessment criteria stated in the KTH appointments procedure, section 1.2., apply in relation to the employment profile laid down. Of highest importance is that the applicant has scientific expertise in the subject field. pedagogical expertise in the subject field. Of second highest importance that the applicant has the ability to cooperate with the outside community for mutual exchange and having acted to ensure that the knowledge and skills found at the university benefit society. expertise in developing and leading activities and staff. For that purpose, the individual is to be knowledgeable about diversity and equal opportunity issues, particularly gender equality. ability to collaborate. It is also important that the applicant has administrative expertise . Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives can be found at KTH's webpage . Application Your application should follow KTH's CV template for employment of teachers . It is the responsibility of the applicant to ensure that the application is complete according to the requirements in the ad and CV template. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply to this position online. For more information regarding KTH's assessement, see Appointments procedure at the Royal Institute of Technology Other For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process please read here. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. Guidance on relocating and settling in at KTH and in Sweden. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Apply here Type of employment Permanent position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100% First day of employment As soon as possible Salary Monthly pay Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3000 Published 27.Oct.2026 Last application date 26.Nov.2026 Contact Johan Kristoffersson +4687909453 jkristo@kth.se Magnus Wiktorsson magwik@kth.se magwik@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/985004?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in Acoustics-Based Traffic Sensing",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in Acoustics-Based Traffic Sensing Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in Acoustics-Based Traffic Sensing KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences Job description Join KTH's research in engineering acoustics at the Marcus Wallenberg Laboratory (MWL) and develop the next generation of acoustics-based traffic sensing. Cost-effective roadside microphones, combined with signal processing and machine learning, can provide continuous, real-time information on traffic flows, vehicle types and traffic noise, whereas cities today rely on short and intrusive measurement campaigns. The position is part of two projects funded by Digital Futures , carried out together with the City of Stockholm, Nacka municipality and other municipalities in the region: a societal innovation project expanding an acoustic sensor network across the Stockholm region, and a proof-of-concept project developing a validated roadside monitoring system. You will build on established testbeds and unique datasets from Stockholm's urban environment. You will deploy acoustic sensor units in urban environments, develop robust methods for detecting and classifying vehicle pass-bys, from processing on the sensor (edge) to the cloud, validate the results against reference measurements, and make data available through APIs and visualisation tools for municipal users. The position also includes scientific publishing, co-supervising students and contributing to new proposals and innovation activities. Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. Strong background in at least two of the following areas: acoustic measurements, signal processing, machine learning, sensor systems or embedded systems. Documented research experience through scientific publications. Good programming skills, for example in Python. Proficiency in English, both written and spoken, as it is used in daily work. As a person, you are curious, independent and motivated by research with practical impact. You demonstrate: Teaching abilities Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality Independence Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Experience with acoustics-based traffic monitoring or with detection and classification of vehicles from sound. Experience deploying sensors or measurement systems in the field over long periods. Experience with machine learning for audio or time-series data, including deployment on edge devices. Experience with data pipelines, databases, APIs or web-based visualisation. Previous collaboration with non-academic stakeholders (municipalities, government agencies, industry). Interest in innovation and in the utilisation of research results. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment 2027-01-11 or according to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3745 Published 30.Oct.2026 Last application date 09.Nov.2026 Contact Romain Rumpler rumpler@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/985017?l=en": {
      "title": "Undergraduate assistent KTH Libary",
      "description": "KTH | Undergraduate assistent KTH Libary kth.se kth.se Student web Intranet kth.se Student web Intranet Login Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Undergraduate assistent KTH Libary KTH Royal Institute of Technology, Support services at KTH Job description KTH is establishing a new Makerspace, which is scheduled to open in February 2027. We are looking for a student assistant to support the development of activities within the Makerspace. The Makerspace is a place where students can develop their skills through hands-on work with tools and machinery. This may involve woodwork, 3D printing, prototype design using various materials, and electronics. The role involves tasks such as: planning and running workshops for the space’s users collaborating with teachers to integrate the use of the space into educational programmes producing training materials and manuals on how to use the space You may also be expected to manage technical equipment and software within the facility, maintain materials and equipment, and help with procurement. Qualifications Requirements You should be admitted to first or second-level cycle education at a  Swedish university Experience in organizing peer groups, student organizations, or volunteer teams. Ability to create structured schedules, rosters, and event workflows. You should be fluent in Swedish and English, for day-to-day work. Preferred qualifications Student at KTH Ability to translate technical processes into clear, written instructions for non-technical users. Experience in liaising with faculty and administration to identify curriculum needs. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives . Application Log into KTH's recruitment system in order to apply for this position. You are responsible to ensure that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application should include the following documents: CV Transcript records Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to 12 months, with access according to agreement. Others For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Part-time Full-time equivalent 50% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 2 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3746 Published 30.Oct.2026 Last application date 10.Nov.2026 Contact Pontus Juth juth@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website This website uses services that may store information about you and how you use the website. Some services are necessary for the website to work, and others are optional. Manage services Accept only necessary services Accept all services"
