    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/955894?l=en": {
      "title": "Undergraduate assistant - Support hardware startups",
      "description": "KTH | Undergraduate assistant - Support hardware startups at KTH Innovation! Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Undergraduate assistant - Support hardware startups at KTH Innovation! KTH Royal Institute of Technology, Support services at KTH Technical Student for KTH Innovation Makerspace – Help Startups Go from Idea to Prototype! KTH Innovation is one of Europe’s leading startup hubs. Each year, we help hundreds of students and researchers explore ideas and launch startups. Our alumni include Blykalla, Airmee, TERASi, SuperAnnotate and Flox, as well as founders behind ventures such as Lovable and Neko Health. An important part of our work is supporting teams developing physical products. That’s where you come in! Your Role We are looking for a student with an interest in, and experience from design and product development who wants a flexible part-time job alongside their studies. You will apply your technical skills, develop your prototyping expertise and gain insight into how startups and early-stage technologies evolve. As a student assistant, you will support teams developing physical products, helping them move from ideas to functional prototypes in the KTH Innovation Makerspace. Your responsibilities include: Providing hands-on and digital support with CAD, 3D printing, laser cutting, basic electronics and prototype fabrication. You will particularly help others use 3D printers effectively and safely. Guiding teams in defining what to test, choosing prototyping methods, planning iterations and evaluating results. Teams remain responsible for their own product development. Introducing teams to the makerspace, its tools and equipment, and helping maintain welcoming, well-organized routines and workflows. You will also contribute to events, study visits and administrative tasks. You will join the KTH Innovation student assistant team and collaborate with KTH's central makerspace, other makerspaces at KTH and student associations working with hardware. The position is 30%, with flexible working hours to accommodate your studies. Some evening events are included. Read more about KTH Innovation Qualifications Required - what is actually needed in the role Admission to a first-, second- or third-cycle programme at a Swedish university. Good spoken and written English as it is needed in daily work. Practical knowledge of CAD software. Experience using 3D printers. Personal Attributes We value inclusion, openness and diversity. You should enjoy helping people with different backgrounds and levels of experience feel welcome and confident in exploring their ideas. You enjoy collaborating with and helping others. You are solution-oriented and can troubleshoot practical technical problems independently. You communicate technical concepts clearly and adapt your guidance to different levels of knowledge. You take responsibility, show initiative and work independently. You contribute to a welcoming environment where everyone feels comfortable asking questions, experimenting and learning. Meriting- desirable, but not all are expected At least one year of studies remaining at KTH. Experience in physical product prototyping and product development. Practical experience building hardware and/or software solutions. Experience with makerspace equipment and manufacturing methods, such as laser cutting, casting, vacuum forming or 3D scanning. Experience from student associations or other organizations connected to hardware and/or startups. Knowledge of electronics. Swedish language skills as it fascilitates daily work. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH Trade union representatives Contact details for trade union representatives . Application Apply through KTH’s recruitment system. As an applicant, you are responsible for making sure your application is complete when submitted. Your complete application must be received by KTH no later than the final day of the application period. Instructions The application must include the following documents: A cover letter (maximum one page) in which you briefly: Explain why you are interested in innovation, prototyping, and the startup environment. Provide a concrete example of something you have built, developed, or prototyped, and describe the tools, methods, or techniques you used. Provide a concrete example of a time you helped someone else solve a technical problem, learn a tool, or make progress on a project. A short CV (maximum one page) that focuses on the requirements and the additional desirable qualifications. Applications that do not follow these instructions may be assessed less favourably. Your application must be received by KTH no later than midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time) on the final application date. About the position The employment is valid for a limited time according to the agreement - for up to one year with a possibility for extension, with a starting date to be agreed upon. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment . It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence KTH as a workplace Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Part-time Full-time equivalent 30% First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-2656 Published 30.Oct.2026 Last application date 15.Nov.2026 Contact Lisa Ericsson 08-7906607 lisaeric@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/984656?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoctoral position in techno-economic analysis of resilient urban energy systems",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoctoral position in techno-economic analysis of resilient urban energy systems Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoctoral position in techno-economic analysis of resilient urban energy systems KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Industrial Engineering and Management Do you want to develop and evaluate concepts for how a brand-new urban district can be supplied with both heat and electricity robustly, even when something unexpected happens, and see your analyses used as decision support by the municipality that will build it? Welcome with your application. The position is part of a collaboration between KTH, Uppsala University and Uppsala Municipality on the energy system in Uppsala’s south-eastern districts. This is one of Sweden’s largest urban development projects, with 21,500 homes planned by 2050. You will work on a real question in a live setting, where your results directly affect how a district is built. Two postdocs are being recruited in parallel to work closely together: one at KTH (this position) and one at Uppsala University. Part of the working time is spent at Uppsala Municipality , which gives direct access to planning documentation, stakeholders and the questions that are current during implementation. The project is part of the research area STandUP for Energy. Job description The position aims to generate and evaluate concepts for the energy supply of Uppsala’s south-eastern districts, and to analyse them techno-economically as decision support for the municipality. Duties include: developing, modelling and comparing concepts for a flexible low-temperature heating system techno-economically evaluating a flexible electricity microgrid analysing the heating system and the electricity microgrid as an integrated multi-energy system quantifying the socio-economic value of the energy system’s resilience analysing the security of supply of the heat and electricity systems during disruptions, and how concept and sizing choices affect recovery time and outage costs developing scenarios for the district’s build-out, connection rates, energy demand, technology rollout and system configuration carrying out techno-economic analyses of the integrated system analysing business models and implementation models for both systems translating the results into decision support publishing results in scientific journals and presenting them at conferences taking part in applications for external research funding, nationally and within the EU Qualifications Requirements A PhD in energy technology, energy systems, mechanical engineering or equivalent, or a foreign degree deemed equivalent. The degree must be completed no later than when the employment decision is made. Documented experience of modelling, optimization and analysis of energy systems, preferably integrated or multi-energy systems Experience of techno-economic analysis, investment planning, infrastructure sizing or operational optimization Knowledge of thermal energy systems, for example district heating, heat pumps or thermal storage Understanding of energy markets and policy instruments, for both heat and electricity Programming skills and experience developing or applying computational models for energy system analysis The ability to express yourself in English, orally and in writing, as English is used daily in the project Personal skills Good collaboration skills and the ability to communicate research results to stakeholders outside academia Goal-oriented and self-driven approach to work Preferred qualification A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline Experience in low-temperature heating systems, waste heat recovery, thermal storage or other distributed energy resources Experience in modelling, optimization or sector coupling of integrated energy systems Experience in resilience or reliability analysis of energy systems, security of supply, or valuation of outage costs Experience in energy economics/business models, or collaboration with municipalities, authorities or industry Commitment to and awareness of gender equality, diversity, and equal opportunities. knowledge of Swedish, or willingness to learn it, for the work with the municipality Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Copy of diplomas and grades from your previous university studies. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Brief account of why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Maximally two pages long. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3737 Published 30.Oct.2026 Last application date 27.Nov.2026 Contact Björn Laumert laumert@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    },
    "https://www.kth.se/lediga-jobb/984227?l=en": {
      "title": "Postdoc in agentic AI for spatial biology of the human gut",
      "description": "KTH | Postdoc in agentic AI for spatial biology of the human gut Skip to main content Studies Studies close Research Research close Collaboration Collaboration close About KTH About KTH close Library Library close Close Studies Close Research Close Collaboration Close About KTH Close Library Close Main menu Close Studies Main menu Close Research Main menu Close Collaboration Main menu Close About KTH Main menu Close Library Search Close Search the KTH website Search Search the Student web Search the Intranet Svenska Menu KTH About KTH Work at KTH Vacancies Vacancies Postdoc in agentic AI for spatial biology of the human gut KTH Royal Institute of Technology, School of Engineering Sciences in Chemistry, Biotechnology and Health Job description How do cells organize into complex human tissues and can AI uncover tissue architecture in health and disease? The Koplev lab at KTH Royal Institute of Technology and SciLifeLab is recruiting an ambitious postdoctoral researcher to lead the development of computational methods, modelling human tissue architecture using single-cell and spatial transcriptomics data. The position is part of a research project funded by Digital Futures in collaboration with Assistant Professor Wei Ouyang's AICell Lab. The project aims to develop autonomous AI scientist systems that perfor end-to-end bioinformatics analysis, including writing and executing code, evaluating results, refining analytical approaches, and generating testable biological hypotheses. A central challenge is establishing how AI agents can be rigorously tested and supervised to enable scientific discovery. The research will focus on human gastrointestinal diseases, including Crohn's disease, ulcerative colitis, and colorectal cancer. The project will develop and evaluate machine learning approaches for identifying cell types, characterizing tissue niches across disease states. The successful candidate will lead computational research projects at the intersection of artificial intelligence, machine learning, and spatial biology. Responsibilities include: Developing and evaluating AI agents for automated analysis of single-cell and spatial transcriptomics data. Integrating large-scale spatial transcriptomics datasets across technologies, tissues, and diseases. Investigating biological mechanisms of tissue organization, including immune cell migration and intercellular signalling. Disseminating research findings through scientific publications, conferences, and open-source software. The successful candidate will join a growing and collaborative research group at the Department of Gene Technology and SciLifeLab. The lab's broader research programme investigates tissue architecture across the gastrointestinal tract, heart, and cardiovascular system, providing opportunities to develop new scientific directions according to the candidate's interests and expertise. The postdoctoral researcher will contribute to the scientific development of the group, including mentoring students and supporting collaborative projects. The position offers opportunities to develop scientific leadership skills and establish an independent research profile in preparation for a future career as a group leader or senior research scientist. More information: https://www.scilifelab.se/researchers/simon-koplev/ Qualifications Requirements A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree. This eligibility requirement must be met no later than the time the employment decision is made. Substantial research expertise in computational biology methods for single-cell or spatial transcriptomics data. Proven scientific excellence as evidenced by strong scientific publications and track record relative to career stage. Experience developing or applying machine learning methods, including deep learning, foundation models, large language models, or autonomous AI agents. Preferred qualifications A doctoral degree or an equivalent foreign degree, obtained within the last three years prior to the application deadline. Highly creative researcher with broad scientific curiosity Mastery of data visualization and scientific communication Exceptional collaborative abilities Self-motivated individual with ability to work independently Teaching and mentorship abilities or interests in personal development Awareness of diversity and equal opportunity issues, with specific focus on gender equality We welcome applicants from diverse backgrounds and with complementary strengths. Great emphasis will be placed on personal skills. Join us at KTH KTH shapes the future through education, research and innovation. As a leading international technical university, we play an active role in advancing the transition towards a sustainable society. At KTH, you have the opportunity to grow and develop in a creative and dynamic environment, with good working conditions and attractive benefits. Equality, diversity and equal opportunities are essential to quality and form an integral part of KTH’s core values as a university and public authority. Learn more about our benefits and what it's like to work and grow at KTH. Trade union representatives Contact information to trade union representatives. To apply for the position Log into KTH's recruitment system to apply for this position. You are responsible for ensuring that your application is complete according to the instructions in the ad. The application must include: CV including relevant professional experience and knowledge. Brief letter of motivation describing why you want to conduct research, your academic interests and how they relate to your previous studies and future goals. Max two pages. Copy of diploma from your PhD. Translations into English or Swedish if the original documents have not been issued in any of these languages. Your complete application must be received at KTH no later than the last day of application, midnight CET/CEST (Central European Time/Central European Summer Time). About the employment The position offered is for, at the most, two years. A position as a postdoctoral fellow is a time-limited qualified appointment focusing mainly on research, intended as a first career step after a dissertation. Other information For information about processing of personal data in the recruitment process. It may be the case that a position at KTH is classified as a security-sensitive role in accordance with the Protective Security Act (2018:585). If this applies to the specific position, a security clearance will be conducted for the applicant in accordance with the same law with the applicant's consent. In such cases, a prerequisite for employment is that the applicant is approved following the security clearance. We firmly decline all contact with staffing and recruitment agencies and job ad salespersons. Disclaimer: In case of discrepancy between the Swedish original and the English translation of the job announcement, the Swedish version takes precedence. Apply here Type of employment Temporary position Contract type Full time Full-time equivalent 100 % First day of employment According to agreement Salary Monthly salary Number of positions 1 Location Stockholm County Stockholms län Country Sweden Reference number PA-2026-3723 Published 30.Oct.2026 Last application date 29.Nov.2026 Contact Simon Koplev koplev@kth.se KTH Study at KTH Research Cooperation About KTH Student at KTH Alumni KTH Intranet Organisation KTH Library KTH Schools Competence centres President and management University Administration Services Timetables Course and programme directory Webmail Learning management system (Canvas) Contact KTH Royal Institute of Technology SE-100 44 Stockholm Sweden +46 8 790 60 00 Contact KTH Work at KTH Press and media About KTH website"
    }
  },
